(7692314, 1260424, 86447, '<td valign="top">You are so brave.<br/> <br/>I can''t imagine taking my camera out in public to shoot strangers... and to shoot someone in pain and get this...   I admire your courage.<br/> <br/>I am so timid with street photography.<br/> <br/>This is well done, Lev!<br/> <br/>Congratulations!<br/></td>', 'You are so brave. I can''t imagine taking my camera out in public to shoot strangers... and to shoot someone in pain and get this...   I admire your courage. I am so timid with street photography. This is well done, Lev! Congratulations!', '2021-04-21 20:54:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692332, 1260555, 4008, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Willem. Nice landscape! I love it when the water is lighter than the sky... us it the blue filter effect here? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks. The effect of the blue filter is mainly on the hills. The dark sky and light water is caused by the other post-processing.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Congrats Willem. Nice landscape! I love it when the water is lighter than the sky... us it the blue filter effect here?   Thanks. The effect of the blue filter is mainly on the hills. The dark sky and light water is caused by the other post-processing.', '2021-04-22 07:52:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692380, 1260692, 28742, '<td valign="top">He looks a bit smug. Maybe it''s stoicism. ;) Super well done, Wendy!</td>', 'He looks a bit smug. Maybe it''s stoicism. ;) Super well done, Wendy!', '2021-04-22 20:37:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692394, 1260692, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Wendy, nice portrait! Has a studio feel, with the background looking like a wall, complete with soft shadows. How did you do that? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>an overlay -- because the background was already weirdly mottled, but not interestingly mottled. And since it was reminding me of a an ink drawing, I liked bringing in a bit of a paper texture</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Congrats Wendy, nice portrait! Has a studio feel, with the background looking like a wall, complete with soft shadows. How did you do that?   an overlay -- because the background was already weirdly mottled, but not interestingly mottled. And since it was reminding me of a an ink drawing, I liked bringing in a bit of a paper texture', '2021-04-22 23:16:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692411, 1260470, 91360, '<td valign="top">wonderful image motti. congrats on new beautiful image.</td>', 'wonderful image motti. congrats on new beautiful image.', '2021-04-23 05:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692488, 1260590, 30049, '<td valign="top">That''s interesting that you see Eastern Bluebirds only in late winter.  We have them year-round here.  Your area looks to be right on the edge of their <a href="https://www.allaboutbirds.org/guide/Eastern_Bluebird/maps-range#" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">breeding range</a>.  We have two active nesting pairs in the front yard currently.  :-)<br/> <br/>As for the scoring on your entry.  One thing that stood out to me immediately was that the eye and beak are not sharp.  That kills a wildlife image pretty quickly.  The composition is a little awkward also with the empty space above the subject.  I like how there is a second one in the background nicely OOF.<br/> <br/>p.s. - I grew up about 45 minutes west of your location.  I always think of home when I see your lighthouse photos.  :-D<br/> <br/>ETA - link.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-04-24 19:58:41.</i></td>', 'That''s interesting that you see Eastern Bluebirds only in late winter.  We have them year-round here.  Your area looks to be right on the edge of their breeding range.  We have two active nesting pairs in the front yard currently.  :-) As for the scoring on your entry.  One thing that stood out to me immediately was that the eye and beak are not sharp.  That kills a wildlife image pretty quickly.  The composition is a little awkward also with the empty space above the subject.  I like how there is a second one in the background nicely OOF. p.s. - I grew up about 45 minutes west of your location.  I always think of home when I see your lighthouse photos.  :-D ETA - link.', '2021-04-24 20:57:47.000000', '2021-04-24 20:58:41.000000', 0),
